From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: airtime queue limits

Now that the AC cores pull their frames from the mac80211 TX queues,
let mac80211 limit the airtime each station has in flight (AQL): it
estimates a frame's airtime when it hands it out and takes it back on
the frame's status, which b43 gives every frame, so the DMA rings no
longer fill with one station's backlog.

On the RT-AC66U B1 (5 GHz ch36/80) with a OnePlus Nord 2 next to it,
downlink TCP with pings from the router during it, alternating with
mac80211's aql_enable: throughput 243/213/229 against 220/234/213
Mbit/s, ping average 28/24/36 against 44/84/34 ms and worst 70/35/78
against 105/179/80 ms.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -7426,6 +7426,15 @@ static int b43_setup_bands(struct b43_wl
 		 */
 		ieee80211_hw_set(hw, TX_AMSDU);
 		ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORT_FAST_XMIT);
+		/*
+		 * Airtime queue limits: mac80211 estimates each frame's
+		 * airtime when it hands it out and takes it back on its
+		 * status, which every frame gets (b43_dma_handle_txstatus(),
+		 * free_descriptor_buffer()), and holds what a station has in
+		 * flight to its limit, so the rings do not fill with one
+		 * station's backlog.
+		 */
+		wiphy_ext_feature_set(hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AQL);
 		hw->max_tx_aggregation_subframes = IEEE80211_MAX_AMPDU_BUF_HT;
 		hw->max_rx_aggregation_subframes = IEEE80211_MAX_AMPDU_BUF_HT;
 		if (have_5ghz_phy) {
